NVK's own mapped device-local memory stays in video memory by default outside WindowServer. NullMoth's own change (not
an upstream Mesa commit).
Device-local memory that NVK itself maps (the shader heap, descriptor tables and descriptor sets, the event and QMD
heaps, USERD, the zero page) was moved to system RAM by the NVRM back end's rule for mappable memory, uncached on the
GPU side, so the GPU fetched shader code and descriptors over PCIe. NVK_LOCAL_MAP_SYSMEM=0 kept it in video memory,
reached through BAR1, where BAR1 covers the whole VRAM; that was opt-in since a stall of WindowServer's channel was
seen with it, and only the Cyberpunk profile set it. It is now the default in every process except WindowServer, for
memory that is not shared with another process or device (exported or imported memory keeps system RAM, as it does for
application memory). WindowServer, the one process the stall was seen in, keeps system RAM as before. The stall has
the shape of the lost doorbell that the read of GPPut through BAR1 before the doorbell fixed later
(nvkmd_nvrm_ctx.c); that the two are the same was not shown on a card.
NVK_LOCAL_MAP_SYSMEM=1 is the way back: system RAM in every process, 3.0's default. NVK_LOCAL_MAP_SYSMEM=0 means what
it meant: video memory in every process, WindowServer and shared memory included. NVK_BAR_VRAM=0, which keeps an
application's own host-visible device-local memory out of BAR1, also keeps the new default off, because the rule would
otherwise place that application memory behind BAR1 again. Where BAR1 does not cover the VRAM nothing changes.
When the RM has no video memory for an allocation the new default placed, the allocation is made in system RAM, as in
release 3.0, instead of failing; one placed by NVK_LOCAL_MAP_SYSMEM=0 or by its caller still fails as before.
The decision is in two functions without side effects (nvrm_local_map_rule, nvrm_local_map_wants_bar), which
tools/test_nvk_local_map.py compiles and holds, and the settings are read once for the process with util_call_once_data
instead of an unguarded static.

